{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"As of **November 6, 2026**, under [Rule 6c-11(a)](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-17/section-270.6c-11), an authorized participant must:\n\n- Be a **member or participant of an SEC-registered clearing agency**.\n- Have a **written agreement with the ETF or one of its service providers** allowing it to place orders to purchase and redeem creation units.\n\nThe rule does **not** require direct membership in both NSCC and DTC or prescribe a distributor-only agreement. Specific NSCC/DTC access and settlement requirements may arise from the applicable agreement and operational arrangements.\n\n**Bank forms:** The reviewed US agreements have not been supplied here, so I cannot verify their actual signatories. Those parties must be identified from the forms—not inferred from the rule’s broader permitted-counterparty definition.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Regulatory AP eligibility and contractual settlement requirements are distinct."}}
